WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:05.560
EPA staffers were shocked to receive this email

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.260
obtained exclusively by CNN.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.920
Which says “we have been directed by the

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.900
administrator to withdraw the restrictions”

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.000
The proposed protection of that pristine area

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.440
was being removed

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.300
Oh no,

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.160
that pristine area,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.380
filled with these gorgeous salmon

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.340
will be obliterated by a mine!

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.660
At least that’s the impression you’d get watching

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.200
CNN’s 2 part “exclusive.”

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.660
I would have believed it except

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.460
I happen to have reported on that mine as part of a

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.640
special for Fox on the green tyranny

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.940
pursued by today’s rich environments.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.440
The proposed Pebble mine is

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.640
a disaster waiting to happen.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.380
That ad comes from one of America’s

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.880
richest environmental groups,

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.440
the NRDC,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.080
the National Resources Defense Council.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.860
Imagine this natural paradise destroyed.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.200
The environmental groups ran these
ads,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.360
they made people believe on TV that everything

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.620
was going to die.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.220
The truth, it turns out,

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.120
is that the mine

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.440
would not even be on Alaska’ Bristol Bay.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.960
The proposed mine, would not even be 10 miles away,

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.600
or 20 miles, or even 50 miles.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.080
It would be 100 miles away!

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.060
Did CNN mention that?

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:20.860
No.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.260
Never.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.300
Instead, CNN made EPA director Scott Pruitt

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.320
look evil by suggesting that right after a

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.280
meeting with the mine’s boss,

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.420
he gave the mine the go-ahead.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.280
He made that decision

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.060
without a briefing from any

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.160
of EPA’s scientists or experts.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.000
What?

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.920
Shocking!

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.900
Without consulting scientists,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.640
Pruitt's going to let a company massacre these fish.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.700
But in fact, he hadn’t given the mine a green light.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.220
He’s simply allowing

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.640
them to submit an official proposal.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.960
Obama’s EPA had rejected the mine

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.100
before it even looked

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.300
at an environmental impact statement.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.240
That’s unheard of.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.480
The EPA normally asks for that environmental research,

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.800
examines it, and then

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.800
accepts or rejects it.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.340
It doesn’t reject things without looking at them.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.140
Pruitt’s allowing the review process to go forward

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.360
was proper.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.000
CNN’s reporter did at least speak with the mine’s CEO,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.280
although he sneered at the boss’s

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.920
reaction to the decision.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.340
“It comes with no apologies"

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.540
"And do you think it was not wrong"

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.000
"that Mr. Pruitt did not even"

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.420
"look at the work even done?”

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.060
“It’s not a science decision. It’s a process decision”

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.160
This looks like the head of a gold mine

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.800
went into a new administrator and got him to reverse

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.480
what an entire department has worked on for years…”

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.440
The reporter was accurate there.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.420
The entire department had worked on killing that mine

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.700
for years.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.120
They had colluded with zealots

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.740
and environmental groups.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.160
Lots of those people want no mines

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.700
built anywhere.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.660
Don’t  believe me?

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.080
Listen to my interview with their spokesman.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.640
There's some mines where NRDC says,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.400
great, go ahead?

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.740
Well, it's not up to us.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:07.600
Are there any?

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.960
It's not up to us to

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.400
green light mines, but what we do is...

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.380
Are there any you don't complain about?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.820
Yeah, sure.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.520
We asked him for some names,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.000
we’re still waiting.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.480
CNN also made claims like this:

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:22.220
The mine could potentially create a footprint

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.520
bigger than the island of Manhattan

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.800
and nearly as deep as the Grand Canyon

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.480
according to the EPA.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.820
It could.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:30.660
But it won’t.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.560
The actual Pebble proposal is much smaller.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.420
Pebble’s CEO is not some monster destroyer of the Earth.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.260
He’s a Democrat who ran

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.860
environment policy for Bill Clinton and Al Gore.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.820
CNN never mentioned that either.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.200
Instead, the reporter called him:

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.140
"A guy who wants to mine gold

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.300
in an area that many scientists believe

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.540
will destroy one of

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.740
the most pristine sock eye salmon sporting grounds

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:57.680
in the whole world?

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.500
What am I missing?”

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.580
“What you’re missing is that if they’re right

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.020
then we won’t get a permit.”

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:04.900
Right.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.960
But explaining that now the mine must

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.860
begin the EPA’s long and detailed environmental review

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.000
wouldn’t fit CNNs theme:

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.620
evil Trump appointee

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.460
ravages the environment.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.600
We asked CNN,

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.000
why didn’t you mention that,

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.400
and that the mine would be 100 miles away?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.140
They didn’t get back to us.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.420
If environmental zealots and their sycophants

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.040
in the media get their way,

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.320
America will be a place with no mining,

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.600
No new pipelines.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.660
No oil drilling.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.180
No… new…anything!

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:37.960
People used say “NIMBY.”

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.300
You can build, just not in my backyard.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.140
Now it’s BANANA.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:46.840
Build-absolutely-nothing-anywhere-near
anybody.

